1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,675
In Hosahalli, the old
school leaks every monsoon.

2
00:00:03,975 --> 00:00:06,997
And now a crack runs right
over a classroom door.

3
00:00:07,347 --> 00:00:08,247
Mrs.

4
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:10,940
Lakshmi, the headmistress,
asks one question.

5
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,752
Will my children be safe?

6
00:00:13,402 --> 00:00:15,714
So the town will build a new school.

7
00:00:15,714 --> 00:00:18,099
Two storeys, for six hundred children.

8
00:00:18,449 --> 00:00:21,246
Ananya, twenty four, is the site engineer.

9
00:00:21,246 --> 00:00:23,139
It is her first big project.

10
00:00:23,488 --> 00:00:25,209
Raghu is the head mason.

11
00:00:25,209 --> 00:00:27,922
Farhan, the surveyor, draws every plan.

12
00:00:27,922 --> 00:00:30,331
Professor Deshpande checks the design.

13
00:00:30,981 --> 00:00:32,813
So what is civil engineering?

14
00:00:33,113 --> 00:00:39,317
In 1828, the Institution of Civil
Engineers got its Royal Charter.

15
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:41,781
It used Thomas Tredgold's words.

16
00:00:41,781 --> 00:00:46,299
The art of directing the great sources
of power in Nature, for the use

17
00:00:46,299 --> 00:00:47,949
and convenience of man.

18
00:00:48,299 --> 00:00:51,509
Nature gives us gravity,
rain, rivers and rock.

19
00:00:51,859 --> 00:00:56,095
In simple words, civil engineers
plan, build and care for the things we

20
00:00:56,095 --> 00:00:56,995
all share.

21
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:01,082
Let's watch the new school take
shape, one branch at a time.

22
00:01:01,432 --> 00:01:02,690
First, surveying.

23
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:06,168
Farhan measures the plot and
marks the levels with pegs.

24
00:01:06,518 --> 00:01:08,558
Next, geotechnical engineering.

25
00:01:08,558 --> 00:01:12,903
A borehole shows the soil layers,
so the footing is sized to suit.

26
00:01:13,253 --> 00:01:15,025
Then structural engineering.

27
00:01:15,025 --> 00:01:19,306
Columns, beams and slabs carry the
load safely down to the footing.

28
00:01:19,656 --> 00:01:24,112
Water and environmental engineering
add a tank, clean water pipes, and

29
00:01:24,112 --> 00:01:26,031
drains to carry waste away.

30
00:01:26,381 --> 00:01:30,736
Transportation engineering plans the
road outside, with a safe bay for

31
00:01:30,736 --> 00:01:31,928
the school bus.

32
00:01:32,278 --> 00:01:35,490
And construction management
turns it all into a schedule.

33
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:37,669
Who works when, and in what order.

34
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:40,604
Every building starts as a problem.

35
00:01:40,604 --> 00:01:43,693
Civil engineers turn it
into a plan that stands.

36
00:01:44,393 --> 00:01:47,458
So civil engineering
has seven main branches.

37
00:01:47,808 --> 00:01:48,708
Structural.

38
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:50,425
Frames that carry loads.

39
00:01:50,725 --> 00:01:51,819
Geotechnical.

40
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:53,813
The soil and rock below.

41
00:01:54,113 --> 00:01:55,260
Transportation.

42
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:57,466
Roads, railways and airports.

43
00:01:57,766 --> 00:01:59,093
Water resources.

44
00:01:59,093 --> 00:02:01,124
Rivers, dams and canals.

45
00:02:01,424 --> 00:02:02,502
Environmental.

46
00:02:02,502 --> 00:02:04,799
Clean water, sewage and waste.

47
00:02:05,099 --> 00:02:07,454
Surveying, also called geomatics.

48
00:02:07,454 --> 00:02:08,904
Measuring the land.

49
00:02:09,204 --> 00:02:10,908
And construction management.

50
00:02:10,908 --> 00:02:12,527
Time, money and people.

51
00:02:12,877 --> 00:02:16,245
Every real project needs
all seven, working together.

52
00:02:16,895 --> 00:02:18,904
Where do these branches work today?

53
00:02:19,254 --> 00:02:20,154
Structural.

54
00:02:20,095 --> 00:02:22,490
Professor Deshpande checks every beam.

55
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:25,962
In a city, engineers design
the frame of a hospital.

56
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:27,315
Geotechnical.

57
00:02:27,315 --> 00:02:29,624
Ananya orders a soil test first.

58
00:02:29,624 --> 00:02:33,918
On a metro line, engineers test
the ground before they tunnel.

59
00:02:34,268 --> 00:02:35,168
Water.

60
00:02:34,875 --> 00:02:37,579
Farhan plans drains for the monsoon rain.

61
00:02:37,579 --> 00:02:41,219
A city water board pipes
clean water to lakhs of homes.

62
00:02:41,569 --> 00:02:42,654
Transportation.

63
00:02:42,654 --> 00:02:45,450
The bus bay keeps children off the road.

64
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:49,281
A highway project plans lanes,
curves and safe junctions.

65
00:02:49,931 --> 00:02:52,490
But is civil engineering always good?

66
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:53,603
Mostly, yes.

67
00:02:53,953 --> 00:02:55,066
The good side.

68
00:02:55,066 --> 00:02:58,703
Safe homes, clean water, and
roads that connect towns.

69
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:00,156
The hard side.

70
00:03:00,156 --> 00:03:04,267
Projects cost a lot, often run
late, and failures hurt people.

71
00:03:04,617 --> 00:03:07,074
Raghu wants to start digging tomorrow.

72
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:09,786
Ananya says, survey and soil test first.

73
00:03:10,136 --> 00:03:11,870
Professor Deshpande agrees.

74
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,490
A few days of tests can save a school.

75
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:19,663
India celebrates Engineers' Day on the
fifteenth of September, the birthday

76
00:03:19,663 --> 00:03:20,604
of Sir M.

77
00:03:20,604 --> 00:03:21,630
Visvesvaraya.

78
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:22,904
The lesson?

79
00:03:22,904 --> 00:03:24,702
Check first, then build.

80
00:03:24,702 --> 00:03:26,500
Safety comes before speed.

81
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:28,050
Quick check.

82
00:03:27,996 --> 00:03:31,045
Which branch checks if the
soil can carry the school?

83
00:03:32,945 --> 00:03:33,955
Geotechnical!

84
00:03:33,955 --> 00:03:37,364
It studies the soil and
rock under every footing.

85
00:03:37,964 --> 00:03:38,977
So, remember.

86
00:03:39,277 --> 00:03:43,475
Civil engineering plans, builds and
cares for the things we all share.

87
00:03:43,825 --> 00:03:48,243
It has seven main branches, from
structures and soil to water, roads and

88
00:03:48,243 --> 00:03:49,143
management.

89
00:03:49,414 --> 00:03:51,678
And every branch puts safety first.

90
00:03:51,678 --> 00:03:53,051
Check, then build.

91
00:03:53,651 --> 00:03:58,294
Next time, we'll look at the parts of a
building, substructure and superstructure.
